 the world and  characters Breaking Bad informs much of  how we viewed Better Call Saul and El  Camino did they change the way we  understand Breaking Bad  and that's why you should re-watch  Breaking Bad that and Vince Gilligan's  Walter White portrayed impeccably by  Brian Cranston all the characters and  actors are amazing but the show does  exist in Walt's orbit his story came  along at the right time his journey is  still relevant and interesting and when  you re-watch knowing how the story ends  you can better appreciate the way the  creators crafted his rise and fall you  might not get the same shock that you  got when you saw some of the series most  exciting moments for the first time but  you can gain a deeper appreciation for  how they were set up and why they work  so well this  is not meth  OD  and to celebrate the 15-year anniversary  of Breaking Bad we're excited to  announce we've teamed up to do a podcast  growth Decay transformation join me and  my co-host Courtney as we travel back in  time to 2008 to revisit one of the most  influential TV shows ever made we'll  have more information coming soon and in  the meantime be sure to follow us on  Twitter at Breaking Bad gdt we'll be  posting updates there and I'll leave a  link to that in the description please  like this video If you enjoyed it please  subscribe to my channel if you haven't  already Go re-watch Breaking Bad and  thanks for watching I'll talk to you  soon  foreign

